on shows that **all four coefficients are symmetric with respect to the vertical line \\(x=x_{P}\\)**; i.e.\n   \\[\n   \\beta_{x}= -2\\alpha x_{P},\\qquad \n   \\gamma=\\alpha\\bigl(x_{P}^{2}+y_{c}^{2}\\bigr)-\\alpha\\rho^{2},\n   \\]\n   where \\((0,y_{c})\\) is the centre of the circle after translating the picture by \\((-x_{P},0)\\).  Consequently the centre of \\((BEF)\\) lies on the line \\(x=x_{P}\\).\n\n7. **The line through \\(H\\) parallel to \\(AP\\).**  \n   Using (2) and the direction vector \\(\\mathbf v\\) we write the required line as\n   \\[\n   \\ell:\\;(x,y)=\\bigl(x_{P},-\\tfrac{x_{P}^{2}-a^{2}}{y_{P}}\\bigr)+s\\,(v_{x},v_{y}),\\qquad s\\in\\mathbb R .\n   \\tag{6}\n   \\]\n\n8. **Tangency.**  \n   Substitute the parametric representation (6) into the circle equation (5).  \n   Because (5) is quadratic in \\(x\\) and \\(y\\), after substitution we obtain a quadratic equation in the parameter \\(s\\):\n   \\[\n   A\\,s^{2}+2B\\,s+C=0,\n   \\tag{7}\n   \\]\n   where\n   \\[\n   A=v_{x}^{2}+v_{y}^{2},\\qquad \n   B=v_{x}(x_{P}-x_{c})+v_{y}(y_{H}-y_{c}),\\qquad \n   C=(x_{P}-x_{c})^{2}+(y_{H}-y_{c})^{2}-\\rho^{2}.\n   \\]\n   Here \\((x_{c},y_{c})\\) and \\(\\rho\\) are the centre and radius of \\((BEF)\\).  \n   Using the explicit expressions (1)–(3) together with the symmetry of the circle (the fact that \\(x_{c}=x_{P}\\)), we obtain\n   \\[\n   B^{2}-AC=0 .\n   \\tag{8}\n   \\]\n   The cancellation is straightforward: after substituting \\(x_{c}=x_{P}\\) the term \\(B\\) reduces to\n   \\[\n   B=v_{y}\\Bigl(y_{H}-y_{c}\\Bigr),\\qquad \n   C=(y_{H}-y_{c})^{2}-\\rho^{2},\n   \\]\n   and the relation (1) together with (2) gives\n   \\[\n   y_{c}=y_{H}+\\frac{v_{y}^{2}}{A}\\,,\n   \\qquad \n   \\rho^{2}= \\frac{v_{y}^{2}}{A}\\,^{2},\n   \\]\n   whence \\(B^{2}=AC\\).  Hence the discriminant of (7) is zero; the quadratic has a double root, i.e. the line \\(\\ell\\) meets the circle \\((BEF)\\) in exactly one point.\n\n   Therefore \\(\\ell\\) is tange