\\[\nC=(-r,0),\\qquad D=(d+R,0).\n\\]\n\nSince \\(CD\\) is horizontal, the perpendicular bisector of \\(CD\\) is the vertical line  \n\n\\[\nx=\\frac{C_{x}+D_{x}}{2}= \\frac{d+R-r}{2}.\n\\]\n\nHence  \n\n\\[\nx_{P}= \\frac{d+R-r}{2}.\n\\tag{3}\n\\]\n\nBecause \\(P\\) is the circumcentre of \\(\\triangle ACD\\) we have \\(PA=PC\\).  \nWriting the equality of the squared distances,\n\n\\[\n(x_{P}-x_{0})^{2}+(y_{P}-y_{0})^{2}=(x_{P}+r)^{2}+y_{P}^{2},\n\\]\n\nand using \\(x_{0}^{2}+y_{0}^{2}=r^{2}\\) from (2), we obtain  \n\n\\[\n-2x_{P}x_{0}-2y_{P}y_{0}=2x_{P}r,\n\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\ny_{P}=-\\frac{x_{P}(r+x_{0})}{y_{0}} .\n\\tag{4}\n\\]\n\nThus  \n\n\\[\nP=\\bigl(x_{P},\\,y_{P}\\bigr),\\qquad \ny_{P}\\text{ given by }(4).\n\\]\n\n**Step 3 – The line \\(AP\\) and the points \\(E,F\\).**  \nSet  \n\n\\[\nv=P-A=(\\Delta x,\\Delta y),\\qquad \n\\Delta x=x_{P}-x_{0},\\;\\Delta y=y_{P}-y_{0}.\n\\]\n\nThe parametric equation of \\(AP\\) is \\(A+t\\,v\\;(t\\in\\mathbb R)\\).  \nBecause \\(A\\) lies on both circles, the second intersection with \\(\\Omega\\) occurs for the non‑zero root of  \n\n\\[\n|A+t\\,v|^{2}=r^{2}.\n\\]\n\nUsing \\(|A|^{2}=r^{2}\\) this quadratic reduces to  \n\n\\[\nt\\bigl(2A\\!\\cdot\\!v+|v|^{2}t\\bigr)=0,\n\\]\n\nhence  \n\n\\[\nt_{E}=-\\frac{2\\,A\\!\\cdot\\!v}{|v|^{2}},\\qquad \nE=A+t_{E}v.\n\\tag{5}\n\\]\n\nIn the same way, substituting \\(A+t\\,v\\) into the equation of \\(\\Gamma\\) gives  \n\n\\[\nt_{F}=-\\frac{2\\,(A-N)\\!\\cdot\\!v}{|v|^{2}},\\qquad \nF=A+t_{F}v.\n\\tag{6}\n\\]\n\n**Step 4 – The orthocentre \\(H\\) of \\(\\triangle PMN\\).**  \nSince \\(M,N\\) lie on the \\(x\\)-axis, the altitude from \\(P\\) to \\(MN\\) is the vertical line \\(x=x_{P}\\).  \nThe altitude from \\(M\\) to \\(PN\\) has slope \\(\\dfrac{d-x_{P}}{y_{P}}\\); its equation is  \n\n\\[\ny=\\frac{d-x_{P}}{y_{P}}\\,x .\n\\]\n\nTheir intersection is  \n\n\\[\nH=\\Bigl(x_{P},\\;\\frac{x_{P}(d-x_{P})}{y_{P}}\\Bigr).\n\\]\n\nUsing (4) to eliminate \\(y_{P}\\) we 